    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) leading the charge as the premier start, buoyed by a prime leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Phillips. His combination of elite sprint speed and a high-efficiency projection makes him our anchor for the scarce stolen base category. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.69) provide the core power upside; while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a modest platoon disadvantage against Rodriguez, his elite 0.450 xwOBA forces him into the lineup regardless. We are also capitalizing on significant platoon edges for **Josh Smith** (62.38) and **Caleb Durbin** (67.85), who both benefit from matchups against mid-rotation arms where their profile fits the high-efficiency threshold for daily volume.\n\nThe bench decision for **Pedro Ramirez** (49.19) was the most difficult, as he hovered just below our 50-point start threshold. He was ultimately squeezed out by the deeper lineup utility provided by **Junior Caminero** (61.33) and the superior efficiency of **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.16) in their respective favorable spots. We are managing the usage of **Colt Keith** (46.34) carefully; while he remains a viable MI option, his matchup against Williams\u2014who currently boasts an elite 2.89 xERA\u2014drastically lowers his floor, forcing us to prioritize safer, high-contact options. We remain mindful of the risk posed by the opposing pitchers today; specifically, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** faces Tolle (3.44 xERA), a formidable arm that limits his upside, though we retain him in the lineup for his situational power potential at home.",
